! mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap -- "IF ANALYZER", printed page 117.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.124, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! EA000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 117".
!
! FORTY-EIGHT LINES, COUNTED NOT ESTIMATED.  The printed LINE column
! runs 1..48 with no gap and the form is blank below line 48.  The
! card-serial column was rendered in two overlapping 600-dpi crops
! and read end to end: EA000001 (line 1) through EA000048 (line 48),
! one serial per line, NO duplicates -- so forty-eight cards for
! forty-eight lines, unlike printed p.112 where a SIC and its branch
! shared a card.
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The serial prefix changes
! to "EA" and the number restarts at 000001; printed p.112 was still
! punching DB0000xx.  The header's own CARD ID repeats line 1's
! serial.
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  Lines 1-3 are an asterisk banner reading
! "IF ANALYZER".  Line 4 is "SLC,$".  Lines 5-48 are forty-four rows
! of straight code in three entry points:
!   S IF AE (line 5)  -- the AE entry: save the lower registers, then
!                        decide whether the interrupted program was
!                        MCP itself (KC,0,MKMCPA / BZXE,M NO MCP),
!                        classify the operation code, and either
!                        branch out to M OP C I / K FRONT or fall
!                        into the common path at M IF 6.
!   S IF AD (line 30) -- the AD entry: save the lower registers,
!                        set S E ("DISABLED IF ENTRY"), and fall in.
!   M IF 6  (line 35) -- the common body: step the IC, pick up the
!                        tentacle table entry (M IF TTT), test the
!                        pseudo-op busy bit against K SUPP2, set the
!                        user bit in the tentacle table, set S L to
!                        MCP, and check S PROG S for the AS register.
!
! >>> S IF AD IS NAMED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE. <<<
! docs/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide (quoted in
! docs/transcription_workflow.md) prints the listing's own statement
! form "(SIC,STIC; B,SIFAD)" -- so SIFAD is the Analysis Guide's
! spelling of this page's line-30 label, letter for letter, and the
! S TIC this page loads twice (lines 9 and 33) is the same STIC.
!
! >>> NINE OF THIS PAGE'S NAMES ARE SETTLED BY A TYPESET PRIMARY
! SOURCE, NOT BY INK. <<<  docs/ocr/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis
! _Guide.txt and its -1 revision are typeset documents, not a drum
! print.  COUNTED, with the counts stated so the claim can be
! checked (base revision / -1 revision):
!     SIFAE  4/4     SIFAD  4/4     SLRMCP 11/11   KSUPP2 2/2
!     MIFTTT 1/1     MNOMCP 1/1     MIFAS  1/1     KFRONT 6/7
! -- eight names, no variant spelling of any of them in either
! revision.  M OP C I IS THE EXCEPTION AND IS SAID PLAINLY: the two
! revisions print it "MOPC1" and "MOPC]1", neither of which is a
! spelling, both of which are the OCR mangling one final character.
! So the Guide corroborates its POSITION (the Type 2 exit) and its
! first five letters, and the final "I" comes from this page's own
! statement column, where lines 15, 17 and 26 print it three times
! and all three compile the same 215630.40.
! The -1 revision's EXITS table FOR THIS VERY ROUTINE prints
!     "SDISP  Error; code in $14 ... Errors possible:
!        Type 1 (MNOMCP) illegal IF interrupt
!        Type 2 (MOPCI)  illegal op code
!        Type 80 (MIFAS) MCP in Auto stack."
!     "KFRONT  $OP is a service op, $1.0 <= OP <= 64"
!     "Address from tentacle table  Legal non-actuator pseudo-op.
!                                   Tentacle linkage set up."
! That table IS lines 13, 15/17/26, 46, 16-19 and 40-48 of this
! page, in order, and it is why no round glyph on this page had to
! be argued from shape: M NO MCP is NO and not NC, M OP C I ends in
! I, and K FRONT's own line 19 comment "-BRANCH IF ACTUATOR OP" is
! the same sentence as the Guide's "$OP is a service op".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE SITS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that printed p.2 opened
! and printed p.98 line 37 closed with "UNTAIL,(2)", so names here
! may legitimately repeat names defined in pp.2-98 at different
! addresses.  That is tail scope and not a collision.
!
! THE ORIGIN IS NOT SET BY A VALUE ON THIS PAGE.  Line 4's card is
! "SLC,$" and the page prints its location as 215470.71 -- word
! 0o215470, bit 0o71 = 57 decimal, i.e. the counter ARRIVED in the
! middle of a word and the SLC rounds it up to the next half-word
! boundary, 215471.00, which is exactly where line 5 is printed.
! This deck writes "SLC, (8)215470.71" for printed p.104's reason: a
! hard SLC assembles standalone and cannot disagree with an arriving
! counter this deck does not have.  When pp.113-116 land, that SLC
! is the row to reconsider -- a bare "SLC,$" would then make the
! join self-checking.  THE ROUND-UP WAS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED: with
! that SLC, strap_asm puts S IF AE at 0o215471.0, S IF AD at
! 0o215510.0 and M IF 6 at 0o215514.0, which are the three printed
! locations.
!
! FROM LINE 5 TO LINE 48 THE PAGE IS CONTIGUOUS -- 215471.00 to
! 215526.40, with no SLC and no gap; every full word is followed by
! the next row one word on and every half word by the next row a
! half word on, and all forty-four locations were checked against
! that chain before a !CHECK was written.
!
! FORWARD JOIN, OBSERVED NOT RESOLVED: line 48 is a half word at
! 215526.00, so the counter leaves this page at 215526.40, while
! strap/mcp_survey.py reads printed p.118's first location as
! 215527.00.  That is half a word apart.  p.118 has not been read
! here and may well open with an SLC or with a line the survey's
! OCR dropped; it is recorded for whoever takes that page and is
! NOT reconciled by guesswork.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one of the 48 line numbers carries the ordinary asterisk
! ("5*", "48*").  THREE lines carry a SECOND asterisk after the
! LOCATION, the unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md 12:
! line 4 (215470.71, the SLC), line 23 (215504.00, "LWF(U),SLRMCP
! +9.0") and line 39 (215517.00, "LF(BU,1),S L,-22").  Lines 23 and
! 39 are ordinary instructions WITH binary printed beside the mark
! and with no gap before them, so the "gap marker" and "SLC marker"
! readings both fail here exactly as they failed on printed p.112.
! Recorded as open, with nothing added to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! HOW THE BINARY WAS SETTLED, AND WHICH ROUND GLYPHS ARE REAL
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This drum opens round glyphs constantly -- this page prints its
! own column heading as "LCCATICN" twice.  Every byte below was
! settled on WHAT PRODUCED IT, against strap/strap_asm.py's encoders
! and their cited sources, never on ink:
!
! * HALF-WORD BRANCH (line 29, "B,M IF 6+.32").  enc_branch_or_misc
!   puts the 19-bit address in bits 0-18 and the code in 19-23; bits
!   24-31 are ZERO for every unconditional branch.  The page prints
!   "215514.50 CO"; the byte is 00 and the C is a damaged 0.
!   (printed p.112 reached the same conclusion for its 28 branches.)
! * BRANCH ON INDICATOR (lines 8, 13, 15, 17, 19, 26).  enc_branch_ind
!   is addr19 | indnum(6) | 1000 | clear | branchOn | idx, so the
!   hex byte CARRIES the indicator's last bit and the 1000 literal
!   and REALLY IS 0xC0 / 0x42 / 0x40 / 0xC6.  These C's are NOT
!   damaged zeros, and they decode:
!     line 13 "215627.32 C0"  indnum 110101 = 53 = XE, branchOn 0 -> BZXE
!     line 15 "215630.74 C0"  indnum 111001 = 57 = RZ, branchOn 0 -> BZRZ
!     line 17 "215630.72 42"  indnum 110100 = 52 = XL, branchOn 1 -> BXL
!     line 26 "215630.72 40"  same XL, branchOn 0            -> BZXL
!     line 19 "220700.32 42"  XL again, branchOn 1           -> BXL
!     line  8 "215474.07 C6"  indnum 001111 = 15 = OP, clear 1,
!                             branchOn 1                     -> BOPZ
!   The same six bytes also settle the ADDRESS's half-word select,
!   which is bit 18, the top bit of the printed two-octal-digit
!   field: .74 and .72 have it set, so M OP C I is at 215630.40 and
!   not 215630.00, and three independent rows agree.
! * IMMEDIATE INDEX (lines 34 and 38, "V-I,2,.32").  enc_imm_index is
!   imm19 | J(4) | 10000 | code(4).  The literal 10000 starts at bit
!   23, so bits 24-27 are 0000 and bits 28-31 are V-I's code 1101:
!   the byte is 0D.  The page prints "CD" and the C is a damaged 0 --
!   but the D is REAL, and is the opcode, not a damaged C.
! * VFL STORE (line 44, "ST(BU,1),.4($1),-22").  enc_vfl_full's last
!   ten bits are code(6) and i2(4); ST's code puts 1101 in bits
!   56-59 and the statement has no "(I')" operand so i2 is 0.  The
!   byte "D0" is real.
! * The OCTAL fields cannot hold a C at all, so every round glyph in
!   a location or in the first two fields of a half word is a 0 with
!   certainty; that is how "COCC03.00", "2155CC.CO" and "215C01.04"
!   were read.  It is NOT used as a licence for any hex byte.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every address below is READ OFF THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY OUTPUT
! COLUMN by inverting the encoder for that row, so a !CHECK on such
! a row tests the opcode and modifier bits and NOT the address
! (listing_oracle's docstring says so).  SEVENTEEN OF THE NINETEEN
! ARE THEN CORROBORATED AT THEIR OWN DEFINING CARDS in
! docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, a garbled full-volume OCR of this
! same PDF used here as a CROSS-CHECK and never as a source:
!
!   215230.00  "S T LR  DRZ(BU,64), 29"            -> S TLR
!   215265.00  "SIC,S T IC" rows on printed p.104  -> S TIC   (and
!              decks/mcp_bootstrap_p112.strap ALREADY SPELLS THIS
!              SYMBOL STIC at this same 215265.00; that spelling is
!              reused here rather than invented, per the brief.)
!   215566.40  "...KMCPA  BAD MCP"                 -> MKMCPA
!   215630.40  "B,M OP CI -INVALID OP" at 226750   -> M OP C I
!   215001.00  "S E   SYN(BU,1),S COM RG"          -> S E
!   215001.04  "S L   SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+0.04
!                     -LEVEL OF INSTRUCTION COUNTER" -> S L
!   215224.00  "S BNDRS  VF,23.0"                  -> S BNDRS
!   215362.00  "S LR MCP DRZ(BU,64), 29"           -> SLRMCP
!   000114.40  "M MAXOP  SYN,SJC1 -MAX PP OP CODE" -> MMAXOP
!   215324.00  "S LR BU  DRZ(BU,64), 29"           -> S LR BU
!   215633.00  "M MK 1   INDMK,.53,255(263)21"     -> M MK 1
!   215666.00  the M IF TTT definition             -> M IF TTT
!   217176.40  "K SUPP2  V,2,32.0"                 -> K SUPP2
!   215546.00  "MR 3AD VF,0.0 -CURRENT TENTACLE
!                              TABLE ADDRESS"      -> MR3 AD
!   215636.00  "M CR  XS IPL IN -CURRENT TENTACLE
!                              TABLE ADDRESS"      -> M CR
!   215021.00  "S PROG S DRZ(BU,64), 2
!                              -PROGRAM STATUS TABLE" -> S PROG S
!   215634.00  "M IF AS  LVI,$14,S IF AS"          -> M IF AS
!   220700.00  "K FRONT  KVI,3,32.0"               -> K FRONT
!
! >>> FIVE OF THEM ARE ALSO CORROBORATED BY DECKS ALREADY LANDED
! IN THIS REPOSITORY, at the same bit, which is a stronger witness
! than the OCR because another transcriber read another page:
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap  SE     SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG
!                                   SL     SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.04
!     and that deck's own !CHECK puts SCOMRG at 215001.00, so its
!     S E is 215001.00 and its S L is 215001.04 -- exactly the two
!     addresses this page's lines 32/45 and 20/39/45 produce.
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap  !SYM SPROGS 215021.00
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110/111/112.strap  STIC SYN, (8)215265.0
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py was run with this deck added to a
! copy of decks/: "950 symbol definitions, no symbol spelled two
! ways".
!
! >>> THIS PAGE CLOSES AN OPEN ITEM ON printed p.111. <<<
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p111.strap line 334 writes
! "SIFAE  SYN, (8)215471.0   ! ONE witness, p.175 'BD,SIFAE'" and
! calls it "THE WEAK ONE, AND IT IS SAID PLAINLY" -- its address
! rested on a single garbled OCR row.  THIS PAGE DEFINES S IF AE,
! and defines it at 215471.00.  p.111's guess was right and is now
! a read definition rather than an inference.  (p.111 spells the
! printed name "S IFA E"; this page prints "S IF AE".  Blanks are
! not significant, both deck spellings are SIFAE, and the two
! agree.)
!
! >>> ONE NAME REPEATS A NAME FROM THE TAIL BLOCK, AND THAT IS NOT
! A COLLISION. <<<  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p19/p28/p29.strap write
! "SLRBU  SYN, (8)2155.0".  Those pages are INSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G"
! block that printed p.98 line 37 closed; this page is outside it,
! and its S LR BU is the 215324.00 word whose own defining card the
! OCR prints as "S LR BU  DRZ(BU,64), 29".  Two scopes, two words,
! one spelling.  RECORDED, NOT "FIXED".
!
! >>> M NO MCP'S ADDRESS IS THE ONE WITH NO SECOND WITNESS. <<<
! The OCR's only legible occurrence of 215627 as a branch target is
